 members left out","note":"Each amount is the debt securities that borrowers resident in the country have issued, at home and abroad, at the amount they will repay, in US dollars at the BIS's exchange rate, so a row can move with the currency without any borrowing or repaying. It already contains that country's international debt securities, and it is part of the total credit books, so these are never added to either. The BIS publishes no world total, so the total is our sum of the countries listed, which leaves out Australia, India, Taiwan and Russia (not covered) and Hong Kong, Philippines, Romania, Saudi Arabia (published by kind of borrower without a total). The euro area is one line, and its member countries are not listed again, so nothing is counted twice; each member has its own book. The book starts in Q4 2020, the first quarter every country listed has a figure; each country's own book goes further back. Source: Bank for International Settlements."}